---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Technology - SkanPay"
  description="Review SkanPay's QR checkout state model, gateway boundary, redemption support, and integration touchpoints."
  activePath="/qr-payments/"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Technology</p>
    <h1>The state model behind QR checkout</h1>
    <p>A technical view of request creation, buyer review, partner handoff, redemption logic, and seller confirmation.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">State model</p>
        <h2>Make every request traceable</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The value is not the QR image alone. It is the request record, state changes, and result that each party can understand.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="state-table">
      <article>
        <span>Created</span>
        <strong>Seller starts request</strong>
        <p>Amount, seller reference, session details, and optional redemption data are prepared.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Scanned</span>
        <strong>Buyer opens request</strong>
        <p>A supported app reads the request and shows the buyer what they are approving.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Decided</span>
        <strong>App returns decision</strong>
        <p>The request can be approved, cancelled, expired, failed, or left pending.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Confirmed</span>
        <strong>Seller receives result</strong>
        <p>The merchant or seller gets a readable result before closing the sale.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Gateway role</p>
        <h2>Coordinate the handoff without hiding the processor</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        SkanPay sits around the request and status layer. Processors and banks remain visible where they handle money movement.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid three">
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Gateway</span>
        <h3>Structure the request</h3>
        <p>Package checkout context so each system knows what action is expected.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Processor</span>
        <h3>Keep money movement explicit</h3>
        <p>Payment processors and banks remain responsible for authorization, clearing, and settlement where applicable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Redemption</span>
        <h3>Validate offers in context</h3>
        <p>Coupon or voucher logic can be coordinated with the checkout request.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Responsibilities</p>
        <h2>Separate seller, buyer, and partner responsibilities</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Clear boundaries make QR checkout easier to support and integrate.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid three">
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Seller</span>
        <h3>Present request and read status</h3>
        <p>The seller needs a clean checkout prompt and an actionable result.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Buyer</span>
        <h3>Review and approve</h3>
        <p>The buyer needs seller details, amount, and a familiar approval experience.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <span>Partner</span>
        <h3>Handle participation</h3>
        <p>Wallet, payment, loyalty, or offer apps need a defined checkout boundary.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section technical-band">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Integration touchpoints</p>
        <h2>Where technical review begins</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Public details stay focused. Partner-specific requirements belong in direct review.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="integration-list">
      <div><span>01</span><strong>QR request format</strong></div>
      <div><span>02</span><strong>Supported app or wallet behavior</strong></div>
      <div><span>03</span><strong>Status and timeout handling</strong></div>
      <div><span>04</span><strong>Coupon or voucher validation</strong></div>
      <div><span>05</span><strong>Merchant confirmation display</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
